    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0892" n="881" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg881"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.00/450b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-27T18:00:00-04:00">April 27, 1937—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Deep concern is felt in important Jewish circles in this country over
                    recommendations believed to be contained in the Report of the Royal Commission
                    of Inquiry<anchor n="2" xml:id="d672-f1"/> into the recent disorders in
                    Palestine. It is feared that the Report will recommend a complete cessation of
                    Jewish immigration into Palestine or some sort of cantonization of the country.
                    The view has been expressed that a prosperous National Home for the Jews in
                    Palestine will serve as a stabilizing factor in the region of the Eastern
                    Mediterranean and that it would therefore be in the interest of Turkey to give
                    moral support to the development of the National Home.</p>
                <p>I would appreciate your considered opinion as to whether views in the above sense
                    would be favorably received by Atatürk<anchor n="3" xml:id="d672-f2"/> if you
                    were instructed to seek an audience for that purpose.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d672-f1" n="2" xml:id="d672-f1-content">
                <p>For the appointment of this Commission and its objectives, see despatch No. 2404,
                    July 31, 1936, from the Ambassador in the United Kingdom, <ref
                        target="frus1936v03#pg_445"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p.
                    445</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d672-f2" n="3" xml:id="d672-f2-content">
                <p>Kemal Atatürk, President of Turkey.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
